r a young  artist award for his turn in the samuel  l jackson sports drama over the next few  years he would star in 2007's emotional  arithmetic 2009's defender and 2011's  real steel but one of his most memorable  experiences was acting alongside anthony  hopkins goyo told light's camera jackson  about working with hopkins who portrayed  thor's father odin he said he is such a  great guy and a legendary movie star  getting the chance to work with someone  like anthony hopkins doesn't come every  day it's certainly something i never  thought i'd get to do  so be it  goyo followed up his role in thor with  an emmy nominated performance in r.l  stein's the haunting hour and would go  on to appear in several more feature  films before he vanished from hollywood  in 2014 those roles included lead parts  and dark skies and the journey home  along with a portrayal of the young  version of russell crowe's noah in the  biblical epic of the same name long  before wyatt olive played stanley yuris  in the it movies and pot loving high  schooler stanley barber in netflix's i  am not okay with this he portrayed the  young peter quill in 2014's guardians of  the galaxy he's since become one of the  brightest young stars in hollywood but  that will come as little surprise to the  people who worked with him on james  gunn's film  crew member simon hatt told the  hollywood reporter have you ever seen  the audition tape of henry thomas for  elliott and e.t  it was like that but way better wyatt's  performance was so real so raw and so  moving i remember being on set and the  whole crew were blown away by him how  did such a young actor turn in such a  convincing performance  he recalled how he felt when his pet  shitsu died olaf said i used that to  help me cry and actually feeling myself  in that situation if that was my mom on  that bed i can feel how powerful that  would be and how awful it would be to  lose someone it wasn't just a one-off  either gunn wanted several takes of the  pivotal scene and oliv nailed them all  hat recalled wyatt gave a stellar  performance with each take he's an  absolute pro and a great collaborator  he's gone bud  abby ryder fortson already had a couple  of credits to her name when she debuted  scott lang's daughter cassie in 2015's  ant-man she had her first tv role in an  episode of the mindy project in 2013  then recurred as ella novak on  transparent during 2014. but she was  still just a shy little girl when she  joined the mcu family speaking to  champagne living ahead of ant-man's  release she discussed her relationship  with paul rudd and revealed that ant-man  and black widow were her favorite  avengers one of the highlights of the  shoot was getting to try on part of the  ant-man suit in wardrobe it sounds like  fortune had an absolute blast on set and  audiences definitely enjoyed her  performance she put in another  scene-stealing turn in the 2018 sequel  ant-man and the wasp by this point she'd  already established herself as a child  star with recurring roles on the spooky  spielberg produced drama the whispers  and hbo comedy togetherness  entertainment weekly dubbed her tv's  most valuable kid though fortune  continues to pop up on the big screen  too her last feature film was 2019's a  dog's journey the post-blip cassie lang  was played by older actor emma furman  but fortune clearly has a bright future  ahead of her  avengers infinity wars ariana greenblatt  was already a child star when she  stepped into the green skin of gamora  daughter of thanos i'm sorry little one  the gifted youngster made her debut in a  2015 episode of disney's live and maddie  making a lifelong friend out of star  dove cameron in the process greenblatt  told entertainment tonight liv and  maddie was my first gig i ever booked  dove has been the sweetest ever since  she's so kind to me and she's like a big  sister you know the future marvel actor  wound up starring in another disney show  taking on the role of mischievous little  sister daphne diaz in stuck in the  middle she appeared in over 50 episodes  between 2016 and 2018 working on her  film resume all the while she made her  movie debut in 2017's a bad mom's  christmas playing the daughter of mila  kunis's bow we may never see her as  gamora again but will definitely be  seeing plenty of green black in the next  couple of years she's in the disney  movie the one and only ivan and the  netflix thriller awake  up and coming young actor kylan davis  actually worked on two marvel films in  2015 one of which was a complete  disaster he played a school bully in  josh trank's much-maligned fantastic  four that same year he also appeared in  ant-man as a member of the family that  gets an unexpected visit from darren  cross aka yellowjacket his scene pops up  in the middle of the big action sequence  at the end of the movie he and his  sister get quite the shock when the  film's villain erupts from their  swimming pool ruining their game of  table tennis and sending their backyard  barbecue into chaos the mississippi-born  actor went on to land a role in matthew  mcconaughey's historical western free  state of jones in 2016. since then he  has managed to carve out a career in  television he played sean campbell and  fox's shots fired in 2017 and followed  that up with a role in the hit netflix  show raising dion in 2019.  more recently he's been seen as jordan  atwater the brother of kevin atwater on  nbc's chicago pd ben sakamoto has  changed dramatically since he made his  debut as hawkeye's eldest son in 2015's  avengers age of ultron cooper barton is  a floppy-haired kid who clings to his  dad when he unexpectedly turns up at the  family safe house with his fellow  avengers in tow the arrow shooting hero  is clearly filled with a deep love for  his wife lara and his kids he goes to  great lengths to keep them safe which  makes it all the more tragic when  they're all turned to dust by thanos we  get to see the fate of hawkeye